{"user": "so is there any tips on how to make a good first move", "user_ts": "2026-08-21T13:35:06.682494+00:00", "assistant": "This board is finished \u2014 no empty squares/legal moves left. Final count looks like **White 42, Black 22**.\n\nFor making a good move in future, use this quick checklist:\n\n1. **Can I take a corner?** Usually yes \u2014 corners can\u2019t be flipped.\n2. **Am I giving White a corner next?** Avoid playing next to empty corners unless forced.\n3. **What legal moves will White have after mine?** Try to leave them few/bad moves.\n4. **Don\u2019t just flip the most discs now.** In endgames, count the likely final result.\n5. **Prefer stable edges/corners over unstable middle flips.**\n\nBest habit: before playing, ask: **\u201cWhat is White\u2019s best reply?\u201d**", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-21T13:35:13.889734+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-21T13:35:16.526480+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Solution Request"], "consensus": ["Solution Request"], "votes": {"Solution Request": 3}, "confidence": {"Solution Request": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Solution Request"], "llama": ["Solution Request"], "sonnet": ["Solution Request"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Board Report", "General Principle"], "consensus": ["Board Report", "General Principle"], "votes": {"Board Report": 3, "General Principle": 3, "Prompt": 1}, "confidence": {"Board Report": 1.0, "General Principle": 1.0, "Prompt": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Board Report", "General Principle", "Prompt"], "llama": ["Board Report", "General Principle"], "sonnet": ["Board Report", "General Principle"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false, "coarse": ["Direct Instruction"]}}
